From: openSUSE packaging
Subject: Ship with telemetry off by default
Patch-mainline: Never, downstream packaging policy
References: https://github.com/zed-industries/zed

Diagnostics and usage metrics default to on upstream. A distribution package
should not enable outbound reporting without the user choosing it; both
remain switchable in the settings UI and in settings.json, so nothing is
removed, only defaulted the other way.

--- a/assets/settings/default.json
+++ b/assets/settings/default.json
@@ -1650,9 +1650,9 @@
   // Control what info is collected by Zed.
   "telemetry": {
     // Send debug info like crash reports.
-    "diagnostics": true,
+    "diagnostics": false,
     // Send anonymized usage data like what languages you're using Zed with.
-    "metrics": true,
+    "metrics": false,
     // Allow sending requests to Anthropic models that cannot be offered with
     // Zero Data Retention
     "anthropic_retention": false,
